                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 2:1",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Now this Amlici had, by his cunning, drawn away much people after him; even so much that they began to be very powerful; and they began to endeavor to establish Amlici to be a king over the people.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "2 Sam. 15:6 (1–10)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 2:2",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Now this was alarming to the people of the church, and also to all those who had not been drawn away after the persuasions of Amlici; for they knew that according to their law that such things must be established by the voice of the people.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 220,
            "end": 225,
            "text": "Mosiah 29:25 (25–27); Alma 4:16 (16–17)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 2:3",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore, if it were possible that Amlici should gain the voice of the people, he, being a wicked man, would deprive them of their rights and privileges of the church; for it was his intent to destroy the church of God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 110,
            "end": 117,
            "text": "Mosiah 29:27; Alma 10:19; Hel. 5:2."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
